<title>MEXICO: Mexico sugar workers' union predicts record crop.</title>
<headline>Mexico sugar workers' union predicts record crop.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-03-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The leader of Mexico's main sugar workers' union predicted Monday that the national 96-97 harvest will produce a record 4.5 million tonne crop.</p>
<p>Enrique Ramos, chairman of National Union of Sugar Workers (STIASRM), said in a statement that yield advancements from mills will enable the country to reach the record figure.</p>
<p>Mexican Sugar Chamber, the umbrella group for sugar mill owners, has predicted this November-June harvest will end at 4.365 million tonnes, down from the record 4.378 million tonnes produced in the 1995-1996 cycle.</p>
<p>((--Chris Aspin, Mexico City newsroom +525 7287902))</p>
